  "answer": "This has been reported before. PowerToys#45712 (v0.97.2, Feb 2026) describes the same behaviour. With the taskbar on the left or top, the Quick Access popup still opens in the bottom-right corner instead of next to the tray icon. It asks for either auto-detection or a setting to choose the corner. A later comment confirms it with the taskbar at the top. That ticket has no fix or workaround, so it is still open as a feature request. Add a 👍 and any details to it. PowerToys#23857 reported the same thing for the earlier tray flyout in 2023, and a maintainer said a hotfix would address it. The behaviour has come back in the current Quick Access, so it isn't fixed there. Until it is, you can open Quick Access with its global shortcut (if you set one in Settings), or move the taskbar back to the bottom."
 },
